/// Year 1 Science's Term 1 (Weeks 1-4): "Exploring Living Things" opens the
/// pathway with a Cambridge-Primary-style spiral for age ~5-6 learners --
/// Week 1 introduces the five senses (sight/hearing/smell/taste/touch) and
/// which sense is used to observe which kind of thing; Week 2 builds on
/// that observational grounding to classify living vs. non-living things
/// using simple, age-appropriate criteria (grows, needs food/water, can
/// move by itself); Week 3 narrows into living things specifically with
/// the parts of a plant (root/stem/leaf/flower) and what a plant needs to
/// grow (sunlight/water/air/soil); Week 4 closes the term with a capstone
/// that explicitly combines all three strands in one story, the same way
/// Year 1 Mathematics's own Week 4 capstone combined its first three
/// weeks. Content was drafted and adversarially fact-checked for
/// scientific accuracy and Burmese translation quality across all four
/// weeks before being wired in.
