/// Term 7: "Push and Pull" (Weeks 25-28) continues Year 1 Science's
/// pathway with a forces-focused strand -- Week 25 introduces push
/// (moves something away from you) and pull (moves something toward
/// you) through everyday actions; Week 26 teaches that a force can
/// start, stop, speed up, slow down, or change the direction of
/// something's motion, and a stronger push/pull generally moves
/// something faster or farther; Week 27 covers floating and sinking as
/// an observed pattern grounded in specific example objects/materials
/// (light materials like wood/rubber/trapped air tend to float, heavy
/// materials like metal/stone tend to sink), deliberately rejecting the
/// "big things always sink, small things always float" misconception;
/// Week 28 closes the term with a capstone combining push/pull, motion
