            "Moe Moe, Nay Chi, and Zaw Zaw plan a class garden bed to bring together everything they learned this term. Moe Moe plants rows of bean seeds, remembering that each seed needs water to begin germinating, with the root growing down first and the shoot growing up second.\n\nNay Chi plants a row of onion bulbs and garlic bulbs next to the beans. \"These will sprout faster,\" she reminds the class, \"because bulbs already store food inside their layers, unlike seeds which need to absorb water first.\"\n\nZaw Zaw is in charge of making sure every plant gets what it needs. He checks that the garden bed gets plenty of sunlight throughout the day, waters everything on a regular schedule, and makes sure the soil is rich with nutrients and that each plant has enough space to grow without crowding its neighbors.\n\nAfter three weeks, the whole class visits the garden. The bean plants have grown tall with strong green leaves, and the onion and garlic bulbs have sprouted lush green shoots even faster than the beans, just as predicted. Their teacher walks through the rows with pride. \"You've combined everything from this term -- how seeds germinate, how bulbs grow differently from seeds, and what every plant needs to stay healthy,\" she says. \"This garden is proof of everything you've learned.\" The three friends promise to keep caring for their garden all year long.",
