            "For a whole year, Kaung Sett kept notes about the weather outside his window in Nova School's garden. From March to May, the hot season baked the ground dry, cracking the soil in the vegetable beds, and Kaung Sett drank far more water than usual just to stay cool. When June arrived, the monsoon rains began, and for months the garden turned lush and green as heavy showers fell almost every afternoon -- Thidar never left home without her umbrella during this rainy season. By November, the rain finally eased, and a cool, dry season settled in, with misty mornings that made Kaung Sett reach for a warm jacket before school. He noticed that each season brought its own weather, its own clothing choices, and even changed what farmers were doing in the fields nearby -- planting during the rains, harvesting as the cool season began. By February, as the cool season faded and the heat began creeping back, Kaung Sett realised his notes had come full circle, ready to record the hot season all over again.",
